\subsection{Diffusion-based Video Editing}

Video editing aims to edit the input video as seamlessly and unobtrusively as possible incorporating the target text descriptions.

The pre-trained text-to-image diffusion models<|CIT-MASK|> have presented an effective solution for generative editing, where earlier works<|CIT-MASK|> in image editing laid the foundation for the development of controlled synthesis of visual information.

Extending the work in image, diffusion-based video editing<|CIT-MASK|> has been attempted based on the video diffusion models<|CIT-MASK|>.

To achieve accurate editing outcomes aligned with the target text, it is crucial to have controlled synthesis capabilities.

Thus, there have been lines of works<|CIT-MASK|> to improve text-conditioned editing controllability. 

To enhance the efficiency of diffusion editing, zero-shot frameworks<|CIT-MASK|> have been proposed.

These frameworks remove the process of training with the input video.

In particular, maintaining video quality across resulting frames is another crucial issue for video editing. 

